  triage:title "ADR-045's own Implementation Evidence table has only 5 rows against ~16 discrete REQ-CORE-RUNTIME-004 behavior bullets" ;
  triage:description "ADR-045's 'Implementation evidence' table (its self-imposed clause-by-clause validation mechanism) has only 5 rows against roughly 16 discrete required-behavior bullets in REQ-CORE-RUNTIME-004: no source-symbol/test mapping exists for audit-event emission, pid_changed semantics, Active/Idle/Offline heartbeat mapping, external-hook mapping, or identity-change/anomaly handling. One existing row ('Remote stripping...') cites the non-specific label 'HTTPS transport regression tests' instead of the real test name (peer_wire_strips_forged_activity_observation_before_routing). Violates AJ.9's own Required Validation rule. Found by req-qa. QA source: PR #744, phase-aj-s9-qa-1." ;
